 {r}←SaveCrashRequest parms;c;d;e;h;m;b;cap;secret;secretQ;saveBody;get;keep;buff;last;note
⍝ HandleError's `customFns` (see `SetErrorParms`): writes what the crashed thread was working on
⍝ next to the crash files, as `<crash>.request.json`, so that a crash caused by an ill-formed or
⍝ unexpected request can be investigated with that request at hand.
⍝ HandleError calls this in the thread that crashed, and Rumba serves every connection in a
⍝ thread of its own, so the thread number identifies the connection: see Rumba's
⍝ `GetConnectionOfThread`. Nothing is written for a thread that is not serving a connection.
⍝ The report holds the connection's last block of data exactly as received, and every message of
⍝ the connection: normally one, more when requests were pipelined. A message that was not fully
⍝ received may lack its request line and parsed headers; then the raw header is reported.
⍝ Values of headers and query parameters that carry credentials are replaced by "***" (see
⍝ `SecretHeaders`, `SecretQueryParms` and `EstablishSecrets`). Request bodies are left out unless
⍝ `[TRAP]SaveRequestBody` is 1, because a body may carry anything; when they are kept they are capped.
⍝ A summary of the request and the name of that file are added to HandleError's `addToMsg`,
⍝ so that the HTML report says what the thread was working on and where the full data is.
⍝ Relies on `G` and `R` being around, just like `AppLog` does.
 r←⍬
 :If 0=⎕NC'G'
 :OrIf 9≠G.⎕NC'Server'
     :Return
 :EndIf
 c←G.Server R.GetConnectionOfThread ⎕TID
 :If ⍬≡c
     :Return
 :EndIf
 cap←65536                                          ⍝ Characters kept of `LastBlock` and of any content
 get←{0<⍺.⎕NC ⍵:⍺⍎⍵ ⋄ ''}                           ⍝ Properties may not exist yet
 secret←∪SecretHeaders,G get'SecretHeaders'          ⍝ `EstablishSecrets` adds those of the INI file
 secretQ←∪SecretQueryParms,G get'SecretQueryParms'
 saveBody←1≡G get'SaveRequestBody'                   ⍝ Default 0
 keep←{(⍺⌊≢⍵)↑⍵}
 d←⎕NS''
 d.Time←A.FormatDateTime ⎕TS
 d.Thread←⎕TID
 d.PeerAddress←c get'PeerAddress'
 d.LastBlockLength←≢c get'LastBlock'
 d.BodiesSaved←saveBody
 buff←c get'LastBlock'
 :If ~saveBody
     buff←DropBody buff
 :EndIf
 d.LastBlock←secretQ MaskQueryString secret MaskSecretHeaders cap keep buff
 d.Messages←⍬
 :For m :In c get'Messages'
     e←⎕NS''
     e.StartLine←secretQ MaskQueryString m get'StartLine'
     e.Method←m get'Method'
     e.RequestTarget←secretQ MaskQueryString m get'RequestTarget'
     :If 0<m.⎕NC'Headers'
         h←m.Headers
         :If 0<≢h
             b←(1 ⎕C⊃¨h)∊secret
             h[⍸b]←{(⊃⍵)'***'}¨b/h
         :EndIf
         e.Headers←h
     :Else
         e.Header←secretQ MaskQueryString secret MaskSecretHeaders m get'Header'  ⍝ Not parsed yet: the raw header
     :EndIf
     e.ContentLength←≢m get'Content'
     e.Content←saveBody/cap keep m get'Content'
     e.(HeaderComplete ContentComplete)←m get¨'HeaderComplete' 'ContentComplete'
     d.Messages,←e
 :EndFor
 ⍝ Note in HandleError's HTML report what the thread was working on, and where the data is.
 ⍝ This happens before the file is written, so that the note survives a failing `⎕NPUT`:
 ⍝ HandleError adds "customFns failed" right after it, which tells the reader there is no file.
 buff←⍬
 :If 0<≢d.Messages
     ⍝ Rumba appends a new message as soon as one is complete (see `GatherRequestMessage`),
     ⍝ so the last message may well be an empty one, waiting for the next request.
     b←0<≢¨{⍵.Method,⍵.RequestTarget}¨d.Messages
     :If ∨/b
         last←⊃¯1↑b/d.Messages                      ⍝ The last one with a request line
     :Else
         last←⊃¯1↑d.Messages
     :EndIf
     :If 0<≢last.Method,last.RequestTarget
         buff,←⊂'request: ',last.Method,' ',last.RequestTarget
     :Else
         buff,←⊂'request: the request line was not received'
     :EndIf
     buff,←⊂'messages: ',⍕≢d.Messages
 :EndIf
 buff,←⊂'peer address: ',d.PeerAddress
 buff,←⊂'last block: ',(⍕d.LastBlockLength),' characters'
 :If ~saveBody
     buff,←⊂'request bodies not saved: see [TRAP]SaveRequestBody'
 :EndIf
 note←⊃{⍺,'; ',⍵}/buff
 note←(⊂note),⊂'Full request in "',parms.crashFilename,'.request.json"'
 parms.addToMsg←((⊆parms get'addToMsg')~⊂''),note
 (⊂(⎕JSON⍠('Compact' 0))d)⎕NPUT(parms.crashFilename,'.request.json')1
⍝Done
